---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contact"
  description="Contact Arizona Pole Vault Academy — (480) 766-6017, arizonapolevaultacademy@gmail.com, 23238 S. Via Del Arroyo, Queen Creek AZ."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Get in touch</p>
      <h1>Contact</h1>
      <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85)">Call to enroll, ask about camps, or plan a visit.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container contact-grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h2>Academy</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Phone:</strong>
          <a href="tel:+14807666017">(480) 766-6017</a>
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Email:</strong>
          <a href="mailto:arizonapolevaultacademy@gmail.com">arizonapolevaultacademy@gmail.com</a>
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Address:</strong><br />
          23238 S. Via Del Arroyo<br />
          Queen Creek, AZ 85142
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          Memberships are typically enrolled by phone. Session reservations happen in the PushPress member app after you join.
        </p>
        <div style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:0.75rem; margin-top: 1rem">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="tel:+14807666017">Call now</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="mailto:arizonapolevaultacademy@gmail.com">Email</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="https://azpva.pushpress.com/open/interested/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Interest form</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="https://azpva.pushpress.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Member App</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="map-placeholder">
        <div>
          <h3>Queen Creek facility</h3>
          <p class="muted">23238 S. Via Del Arroyo · Queen Creek, AZ 85142</p>
          <p>
            <a
              class="btn btn-secondary"
              href="https://maps.google.com/?q=23238+S.+Via+Del+Arroyo,+Queen+Creek,+AZ+85142"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              Open in Google Maps
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0" id="parking">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--red)">Visit</p>
          <h2>Where to park</h2>
          <p class="muted">Use this diagram when you arrive at the Queen Creek facility.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="card" style="padding: 1rem">
        <img
          src="/images/where-to-go.png"
          alt="Map showing where to go and park at Arizona Pole Vault Academy"
          class="parking-map"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption class="muted" style="margin-top: 0.75rem">
          Parking and arrival diagram for 23238 S. Via Del Arroyo, Queen Creek, AZ 85142.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0" id="bad-weather-parking">
    <div class="container prose" style="max-width: 75ch">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--red)">Protocol</p>
      <h2>Bad weather parking protocol</h2>
      <p>
        When the horse arena (our usual parking lot) is flooded, we use a tighter parking plan to reduce congestion
        on the blacktop and neighborhood streets. We keep a low profile out of respect for our neighbors.
      </p>
      <h3>What to do when the arena is out of commission</h3>
      <ul class="list-check">
        <li><strong>Carpool if possible.</strong> We try to send a heads-up ahead of time when we can.</li>
        <li><strong>Drop off and pick up in front of our property.</strong> Do not pull down the driveway — that can create a traffic jam.</li>
        <li><strong>Early vault practice:</strong> leave promptly when your session ends so the next group can park.</li>
        <li><strong>Park efficiently.</strong> Pull all the way forward and avoid leaving large gaps between cars.</li>
        <li><strong>Allowed parking:</strong> in front of our property (okay to block trailers) and in our front courtyard.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Never park or wait on or in front of a neighbor’s property</strong> — including when the arena is open.
        All waiting should be done in front of our property only.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        During flooded-arena periods we may also reduce AZPVA clinic spots (for example from 30 to 20) and adjust
        related weight-lifting club sessions as needed. Thank you for helping us be good neighbors.
      </p>
      <p>
        Questions? Call <a href="tel:+14807666017"><strong>(480) 766-6017</strong></a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
